      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Metal fume fever (MFF) is an acute self-limited, flu-like illness resulting from inhalation of metal oxides. Despite the well-documented history of MFF in the medical literature, the illness may remain unrecognized because it may mimic a viral illness. The case of a patient with MFF due to galvanized steel welding presenting to the emergency room is described."},
